<article class="env-remark" id="032C">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/032C">Remark <span data-tag="032C">10.160.9</span>.</a> If $k$ is a field then the power series ring $k[[X_1, \ldots , X_ d]]$ is a Noetherian complete local regular ring of dimension $d$. If $\Lambda $ is a Cohen ring then $\Lambda [[X_1, \ldots , X_ d]]$ is a complete local Noetherian regular ring of dimension $d + 1$. Hence the Cohen structure theorem implies that any Noetherian complete local ring is a quotient of a regular local ring. In particular we see that a Noetherian complete local ring is universally catenary, see Lemma <a href="/tag/00NM" data-tag="00NM">10.105.9</a> and Lemma <a href="/tag/00NQ" data-tag="00NQ">10.106.3</a>. </p>
</article>